 36MG c  One-proton knockout reaction                                           
 36MG c  2013Do22: levels and gamma rays in {+36}Mg populated via one-proton    
 36MG2c  knockout reaction with a thick carbon target. Radioactive beam         
 36MG3c  of {+37}Al at 247 MeV/nucleon was produced from fragmentation of       
 36MG5c  {+48}Ca beam at 345 MeV/nucleon with Be target at RIBF-RIKEN facility. 
 36MG6c  Secondary beam was purified via B|r-|DE-B|p method and identified by   
 36MG7c  |DE-B|r-tof method using BigRIPS separator. Gamma rays were detected in
 36MG8c  coincidence with {+36}Mg particles using DALI2 array of 186 large-     
 36MG9c  volume NaI(Tl) detectors. Deduced levels, J, |p. Comparison with       
 36MGAc  shell-model calculations                                               
